  "_readme": "Apex portal user store. 'email' is both the portal identity and the JWT 'sub' — it must EXACTLY match a Tableau Cloud username on the site (add each as Viewer). Every entry in 'attributes' is injected into the Connected App JWT as a user attribute claim and can be read in Tableau with USERATTRIBUTE / USERATTRIBUTEINCLUDES (names are case sensitive). 'client name' must EXACTLY match [Client Name] in the data; 'subscription tier' matches [Subscription Tier] (Premium / Standard). 'service line' and 'engagement type' list exactly what the user may see and must EXACTLY match [Service Line] / [Engagement Type] in the data (a user missing either sees nothing); multiple 'client name' values span several clients. 'persona' is a display label. 'roles': ['activity'] grants the portal activity log page.",
